\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S1}{\ignorespaces Fragility functions used in the hypergraph network modelling, modified from Dunant et al. (2025). Each panel shows the functions for a different building type in the METEOR dataset, relating peak ground acceleration (PGA, in g) to the probability of a complete damage state. Note that each fragility function is defined by two parameters: a scale parameter that sets the PGA value for a 50\% probability of complete damage, and a standard deviation (std) that defines the spread of the curve. Parameter values and sources for the fragility curves are included in the plots and in the references.}}{34}{figure.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
